# Heartbeats — monetization floor

216labs needs **revenue** to cover API tokens, hosting, and model spend. Technical heartbeats (errors, deploy, GHCR) are necessary but not sufficient.

## Read this first

**The binding constraint is distribution, not payment plumbing.** Measured 2026-08-15 across every
retained access log: **34 human visitors in 4 months, 4 in the last 30 days, 0 in the last 7** —
whole portfolio, plus 0 waitlist signups and 0 leads ever. See
`docs/REVENUE-STRATEGY.md`. Between 2026-05-29 and 2026-08-15 every production snapshot named
"first StoryMagic sale — blocked on CEO Stripe Payment Link" as the top priority. That was wrong:
a checkout converts a fraction of visitors, and any fraction of zero is zero.

## Cadence

- **At least 1 in every 10 heartbeats** should materially advance **making money** (not a status-only mention).
- When the random `[Reflect]` prompt is revenue-themed (see `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/lib/heartbeat_harness.json`), treat that cycle as the monetization beat: **prioritize a shippable revenue path** unless production is on fire.

## Check before doing revenue work

Open [admin → Org metrics](https://admin.6cubed.app/org-metrics) and read **Human visitors (7d)**
(humans only; bots are excluded since the `is_bot` rollup landed).

- **Human visitors ≈ 0** → the beat must advance **distribution or a non-traffic revenue path**. Payment/pricing/paywall work does **not** count.
- **Human visitors > 0 and growing** → conversion work counts again: checkout, pricing, paid tier.

## What counts when human visitors are ~0

- Anything that puts a real product in front of a real stranger: outbound, a published piece with a distribution plan, a listing/directory submission, a partner or client conversation.
- Service and consulting revenue — needs one buyer, not a thousand visitors. Currently the highest-EV path (`docs/REVENUE-STRATEGY.md`).
- Telegram **`/work`** (alias **`/firstsale`**) is the CEO outbound: a forwardable hire + CARFAC blurb. Do not restore Payment Link copy there while humans ≈ 0.
- Admin **Overview** (`FirstSaleBanner`, `RevenueNextStepCard`) must match `/work` while humans ≈ 0. Do not restore Payment Link as the default dashboard CTA.
- Turning existing research (CARFAC audio, birdperch) into a **paid pilot, grant, or client offer**. The public Colabs and `docs/CARFAC-PILOTS.md` are that offer — keep the hire link on those surfaces; do not hide it behind the blog or landing only.
- Public hire/proof surfaces (landing `#work`, blog cards) must stay visible when sibling apps are cold. Do not leave the homepage empty behind activator warmup.
- A **502 on a host that already had humans** (today: `anchor.6cubed.app`, `zurichrunclubs.6cubed.app`) is a distribution bug. Fix Caddy/warmup; a 302 to activator is not finished until the dest returns **200**. If those hosts already return **200**, the next beat is a visitor-facing fix on the live page (fake data, placeholder copy, dead links)—not another warmup writeup. **Curl the public HTML** for the new string before marking shipped. `zurichrunclubs` is excluded from periodic GHCR sync — `SYNC_SERVICE=zurichrunclubs` pulls that service only. If `/` already has CityRunning (~60k Next HTML), change Anchor or landing, not the timetable again.
- Public audio/ML proof dest is the GitHub colab README (`colabs/carfac-sai-underwater`), not `blog.6cubed.app` — that host is usually cold (302). Do not start blog or agitweet to verify the offer. If a leftover blog deep link is kept, Activator `dest` must preserve the path (a dest that strips to the origin dumps the buyer on the index).
- Qualified-lead inbox that does not need the CEO: [paid-pilot issue](https://github.com/6cubed/216labs/issues/new?template=paid-pilot.yml). Prefer that over another landing `#work` restyle. Do not start merch/marketing to repair a shop card — remove the cold link.
- Measurement that changes a decision — but only once. Do not rebuild dashboards every beat.

## What does not count

- Wiring Stripe keys, Payment Links, pricing pages, paywalls, or affiliate tags **while nobody is visiting**.
- **Building another app.** 72 apps, 10 enabled, ~0 visitors, €0 revenue. App #73 has negative expected value.
- Error reporting, deploy scripts, GHCR matrix, or probe lists **unless** they unblock a paid launch this week.
- "We should monetize someday" without a commit, deploy, or concrete next move.
- Restyling the hire funnel (landing/admin/Telegram `/work`, Caddy dest, blog cards) when the latest closeout snapshot already says **CEO send /work**. That is BLOCKED (CEO). Reach a stranger some other way, or fix something actually broken.
- Re-posting the same hire blurb to Agitweet every beat, or `--force-recreate agitweet` when the volume sqlite already has `6cubed.app/#work`. A public 302 to activator means the app is cold — do not wake it to re-check. One live hire post is enough; the next beat is a stranger or a non-funnel fix.

## When blocked

Name the blocker and the **next concrete move**. If the blocker is the open strategy decision
(services vs audio/ML consulting vs one consumer product), say so and pick the smallest reversible
step that is useful under either choice — do not fall back to checkout plumbing to feel productive.
